  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Start Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - It is time to use what you have made so far and create the ENCODER!
  - The ENCODER takes the output embedding of the POSITIONAL ENCODER and ENCODES
    the embedding to represent the contextual, semantic, and syntactic meaning instead
    of the original resources themselves.
  - This is done by first adding the output of ATTENTION to the embedding to add
    semantic information. Then a NEURAL NETWORK embeds it further to properly represent
    the context added by the ATTENTION in the embedding.
  - The first steps to making the ENCODER is to use the POSITIONAL ENCODER that you
    made on the first factory floor and use that embedding in an ATTENTION FACTORY.
  - Don't forget to duplicate an additional copy of the initial embedding before
    the ATTENTION, as you will need the unaltered embedding in the next step!
